# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI / discovery backends (SECRETS — never commit real values; set them in
# Supabase secrets for the edge functions, or in the shell env for the CLI
# harness `node scripts/trace-username.mjs`). Tried in this order:
#
# 1. OpenAI-compatible unified proxy (pools many free-tier providers, so one
#    exhausted quota fails over to the next). Grounded discovery pins
#    AI_PROXY_SEARCH_MODEL, which MUST route to Google for real grounding.
#    A localhost URL only works on the machine running the proxy — production
#    needs a cloud-reachable URL or the direct keys below instead.
# AI_PROXY_BASE_URL=""
# AI_PROXY_API_KEY=""
# AI_PROXY_MODEL="auto"
# AI_PROXY_SEARCH_MODEL="gemini-2.5-flash"
#
# 2. Google Gemini direct (google_search grounding).
# GEMINI_API_KEY=""
#
# 3. Anthropic direct (web_search).
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""
#
# Google Programmable Search — separate quota, preferred discovery backend
# when set (the literal Google index, no AI in the loop).
# GOOGLE_CSE_KEY=""
# GOOGLE_CSE_ID=""
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# School-based fallback (players with no online USCF tournament history).
#
# Chess.com friends lists are member-public but the endpoint requires a
# logged-in session, so the school resolver reads them server-side with a
# session cookie. The resolver reads the cookie from the `chess_cookies`
# Supabase table first (kept fresh by the scheduled refresher below) and falls
# back to this env var for local dev / before the first refresh. Copy the
# `Cookie:` header from a logged-in chess.com request (dev-tools → Network) —
# PHPSESSID is the important part. Without any cookie the crawler falls back to
# the fully public game-overlap + club signals.
# CHESSCOM_COOKIE=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Automatic Chess.com cookie refresher (api/refresh-chess-cookie, Vercel cron).
#
# A scheduled Vercel function keeps the session above alive so CHESSCOM_COOKIE
# never has to be re-pasted by hand. Set these in the VERCEL project env:
#
#   • CHESS_COM_USERNAME / CHESS_COM_PASSWORD — the service account creds. Used
#     for a best-effort credential login. NOTE: chess.com's /login is protected
#     by Cloudflare Turnstile, so a fully-headless login is often rejected — the
#     RELIABLE path is keep-alive: seed CHESSCOM_COOKIE once from a real browser
#     session and the cron extends it before it expires.
#   • CHESSCOM_COOKIE — the one-time browser-session seed (same var as above).
#   • SUPABASE_URL + SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY — where the refreshed cookie is
#     stored/read (the `chess_cookies` table is RLS-locked to the service role).
#   • CRON_SECRET — recommended; Vercel Cron sends it as
#     `Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>` and the function rejects calls that
#     don't match, so the endpoint can't be triggered by the public.
#   • CHESSCOM_TURNSTILE_TOKEN — OPTIONAL. A Turnstile token if you can supply
#     one out of band. This project never solves/bypasses the bot-check itself.
#
# The cron schedule lives in vercel.json (hourly). More-frequent schedules need
# a Vercel plan that permits them.
# CHESS_COM_USERNAME=""
# CHESS_COM_PASSWORD=""
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=""
# CRON_SECRET=""
# CHESSCOM_TURNSTILE_TOKEN=""
